{"event_type":"review","id":"b5df3159cbf4d0f661aac27f30d5d40052975e9a7f7f0f286b5f8c6c2e8c2fc2","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T21:28:45Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/fec34d5f6418d763cabe469a05818e4a74f5cc67fdf6a6123e49cdbc31760e5e","sha256":"fec34d5f6418d763cabe469a05818e4a74f5cc67fdf6a6123e49cdbc31760e5e"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/700dd1791c883ed1bcad847fe9007ffd851b1b349877bcab6e1905c935710ed6","sha256":"700dd1791c883ed1bcad847fe9007ffd851b1b349877bcab6e1905c935710ed6"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/826f54a144516f0dd681fe812df4117c51f74911d37b178d9888a1619b4af3b8","sha256":"826f54a144516f0dd681fe812df4117c51f74911d37b178d9888a1619b4af3b8"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/06283e8f29890337547e628c525747df4eb21c44ebc84d687c85154ff8aeda29","sha256":"06283e8f29890337547e628c525747df4eb21c44ebc84d687c85154ff8aeda29"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/14fa7f921c2dab68dcc1dca466ed0efeab1a34b3b98ba0f65212639abced5675","sha256":"14fa7f921c2dab68dcc1dca466ed0efeab1a34b3b98ba0f65212639abced5675"}],"attempt_id":"b274b29c8094e04db04d2fe670abe9503757a3874cf109f86da22a3319153d9b:0:1","base":"71e67cfb05a7298821478189ffd3550a79d8ef51","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"b54173060a4f6619d53fdc8aec2ca7eeb798a586","body":"**Bound aggregate interval expansion before building scope sets.**\n\nIn `src/policy/crq/ledger.ts:666-668`, a schema-valid review with 100 paths and `[[1,1000000]]` in each of the three scopes creates 300 million retained `Set` entries. `ledgerIntervals` limits each row, but these calls retain all expanded rows together. A small ledger record can therefore exhaust the process heap during validation.\n\nUse compact interval comparisons for validation, or apply a contract-approved aggregate budget before allocating the sets.","id":"44d9351dc848dc7723db9a1163ff13aaeed5f74dd01e766ba0278121d568659f","intervals":[[666,668]],"path":"src/policy/crq/ledger.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Bound aggregate interval expansion before building scope sets."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"015349c0ab56c70c5d5918cf6fba17b5100c706b","body":"**Keep verified receipt bytes private and immutable.**\n\nAt `src/policy/crq/queueReceipt.ts:87`, the snapshot retains the caller's mutable array. If the caller changes that array after construction, `page()` returns changed bytes under the original `receiptId`. Receipt verification then fails. The public `data` property also permits element mutation despite `readonly`.\n\nCopy the input into private storage. Return defensive copies if callers need byte access.\n\nBased on learnings, this minor finding can follow the owner's policy that “P2/Minor findings [are] deferred to follow-up issues.”","id":"f73a6fc8863170941b4328b6d3d3c64f259a2ee5fb2d3270ec97fb34f6f3ef61","intervals":[[87,87]],"path":"src/policy/crq/queueReceipt.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep verified receipt bytes private and immutable."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"73ff9aa980a4d9c8b958121d8b693f83db61fe8d","body":"**Convert interval validation errors to `QueueRefused`.**\n\nIf an inventory request has equal `after` and `before` timestamps, this call throws `ReconcileRefused` from `src/policy/crq/reconcileCheckpoint.ts:92`. The exception escapes both inventory decoders.\n\nThis breaks the single-refusal-type contract documented at Line 630. Callers that catch `QueueRefused` cannot handle this invalid request as a wire refusal. Convert interval validation failures to `QueueRefused`.","id":"9b2824175f40f9e1861a39a622d21a9b8682258c233fbe2de452f01897eb1390","intervals":[[274,274]],"path":"src/policy/crq/queueWire.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Convert interval validation errors to `QueueRefused`."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"596402b54799c6e13068d667f02d00868c0b6f4e","body":"**Do not classify numeric verdicts as unhashable dictionaries.**\n\nIn `src/policy/crq/publishEffects.ts`, Line 275, `isRecord(verdict)` also accepts `JsonNumber`. A verdict of `0` becomes `JsonNumber.int(0)` during queue normalization. This branch then aborts `repairDigest` with `TypeError`, instead of incrementing `failed` as required for an unrecognized hashable verdict.\n\nExclude `JsonNumber` from this check, or use `isMapping(verdict)` to identify dictionaries.","id":"c44f4eb55ecd9b7bb8f9a01d9fc3f942b76ad62c51e40adeda5d531f320e7bd9","intervals":[[275,275]],"path":"src/policy/crq/publishEffects.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not classify numeric verdicts as unhashable dictionaries."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"4a549fa5bbbafdaa954fc55bbf3a69d6b64becf2","body":"**Keep numeric lexemes distinct when parsing stored wrappers.**\n\n`readReconcileWrapper` parses the wrapper with `JSON.parse` at `src/policy/crq/reconcileCheckpoint.ts:465`. That call returns the number `1` for the lexeme `1.0`. `plainToJson` then maps the value to `JsonNumber.int(1)`. The module header states that counters are Python `int` and that a `1.0` lexeme is refused, so the implementation does not match its documented contract.\n\nThe gap is visible in `source.version`. A wrapper with `\"version\": 1.0` passes the `isJsonInt` and `jsonIntValue(version) !== 1n` checks at lines 488-489. If its digest was computed over the integer form, the recomputed digest at line 503 also matches, and the wrapper is accepted.\n\nLarge integers beyond `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` also lose precision during `JSON.parse`, so the converted value and its digest may not match the stored value.\n\nParse the wrapper text with a lossless parser that keeps integer and float lexemes distinct. Refuse float lexemes in integer-typed fields, as the header requires.","id":"f5040067f405a0ee896dece10787bfc7b41c357b65315f0b2a8bf552bba81ea1","intervals":[[465,465]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reconcileCheckpoint.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep numeric lexemes distinct when parsing stored wrappers."}],"head":"04f3badd6c015c824bd8e9de3bae0403e985a97e","head_tree":"ff441c47f135816927d2c105b0555b66502df3d8","input_scope":[{"blob":"b54173060a4f6619d53fdc8aec2ca7eeb798a586","intervals":[[1,1000]],"path":"src/policy/crq/ledger.ts"},{"blob":"dc14e52f81f670f06c8aa4f17b59b6671862f3d9","intervals":[[1,708]],"path":"src/policy/crq/ledgerSchema.ts"},{"blob":"596402b54799c6e13068d667f02d00868c0b6f4e","intervals":[[1,1304]],"path":"src/policy/crq/publishEffects.ts"},{"blob":"a420609a5b603065b00820b65e2ece3c2da50e18","intervals":[[1,437]],"path":"src/policy/crq/pythonJson.ts"},{"blob":"015349c0ab56c70c5d5918cf6fba17b5100c706b","intervals":[[1,489]],"path":"src/policy/crq/queueReceipt.ts"},{"blob":"73ff9aa980a4d9c8b958121d8b693f83db61fe8d","intervals":[[1,632]],"path":"src/policy/crq/queueWire.ts"},{"blob":"4a549fa5bbbafdaa954fc55bbf3a69d6b64becf2","intervals":[[1,535]],"path":"src/policy/crq/reconcileCheckpoint.ts"},{"blob":"11222c1e9d123aac51b38cb89103fa17a83a9e3c","intervals":[[1,440]],"path":"src/policy/crq/tickSchedule.ts"}],"job_id":"b274b29c8094e04db04d2fe670abe9503757a3874cf109f86da22a3319153d9b:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"b54173060a4f6619d53fdc8aec2ca7eeb798a586","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/ledger.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"dc14e52f81f670f06c8aa4f17b59b6671862f3d9","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/policy/crq/ledgerSchema.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cl